findings.citation_text:
4-602.13 The following nonfood contact surfaces were observed to be soiled:
A) surfaces under/between steamers (food debris);
B) inside cabinets under handsinks (splash/general buildup); 
C) lower shelves throughout (general buildup);  and
D) floor fan at drive thru side of make line (dust).
Nonfood contact surfaces shall be cleaned at a frequency necessary to eliminate buildup of grease, food splash and general debris.

findings.comment:
750.800e - The following non-food contact surfaces were soiled: 
A) surfaces between drive thru soda machine and handsink (splash & old plastic covering);
B) warmers - bottom inside, gaskets, & shelves (food debris/general buildup);
C) ledges where rectangle sanitizer solution containers rest (crumbs);  
D) sprayer surface (buildup);   and
E) plumbing under 3 part sink (buildup).

Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.

findings.citation_text:
750.1220 - Floors along walls and in corners were observed to be soiled with buildup of food and/or single service articles and general debris in the following areas:
A) under lobby drink counter;
B) behind warmers and storage shelving at end of make line;
C) under spare make line at drive thru;  and
D) under drive thru soda machine and handsink counters.

Floors shall be maintained clean. Clean floors in the aforementioned areas.
